{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/503073-on-line-gaming-seems-to-lack-mechanical-support","id":503073,"title":"On line gaming seems to lack mechanical support","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-04T10:41:49-07:00","id":503073,"title":"On line gaming seems to lack mechanical support","content":"I see lots of stuff out there that is for the antiquated system we old fogies got when Star Wars first hit the big screen. I see nothing centered in supporting Storyteller based mechanics from the get go. Is this because that company absconded with and then destroyed our original gaming producer? Are they the hold up on developing something that would support the fan base? Is there anyway to reclaim our game? I am attempting to be civil about this, though I must confess my feelings about this are anything but. I apologize if I am in the wrong here.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I think I know how a Solubri Blood Doll must have felt after their merger with House Tremere.<br /> <br /> Sincerely,<br /> <br /> Whithers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":". 05-05-2015, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T19:21:09-07:00","id":506332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div cla