rt. There are programs out there for Pathfinder, D&amp;D, and D20 based games but nothing for Storytelling. I can only guess that this is because no one has or because no one is allowed to provide supportive programming. I really hope it is not the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T14:59:30-07:00","id":724237,"title":"","content":"I'm still confused. What kind of programs are you looking for? An MMO? Voice chat groups? websites that run the game via chat or forum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T15:05:55-07:00","id":724243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whithers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/503073-on-line-gaming-seems-to-lack-mechanical-support?p=724158#post724158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I have been away for awhile. I mean there is no online support. There are programs out there for Pathfinder, D&amp;D, and D20 based games but nothing for Storytelling. I can only guess that this is because no one has or because no one is allowed to provide supportive programming. I really hope it is not the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sorry, I still don't quite get what it is you are looking or. What support do you require exactly? Maybe we can point you in the right direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mattb7540","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4675-mattb7540","name":"mattb7540","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4675_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T08:36:02-07:00","id":726087,"title":"","content":"Everything for assisting what is now called Table Top play (which used to mean die cut board games like Third Reich or Fortress Europa), instead of Pen and Paper, is pretty much for things that are associated with or related to D&amp;D. Anything that is out there, such as Table Top Simulator on Steam, requires that you completely create your own programmed packs to support the gaming system and lacks the input needed to support the ST system. Something that integrates VOIP, controlled screen sharing - ie. the ST could use Google Maps in a shared viewer to show the group where they are located or the street view of their location. I think that is just about world wide at this point. (Ok, their detail in N. Korea appears a bit limited but Tokyo was passable.) Shared character sheets, NPC sheets, etc. Setting sound files for special effects, mood music, etc. through a Skype like program for RPing specifically in the Storyteller system. There could be options to turn it off for those whose computers can't handle a specific thing or do better with less, but overall when it comes to my favorite system I spent over a year looking for something out there that I would be able to use and there is nothing out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T22:23:02-08:00","id":750718,"title":"","content":"I know exactly what you mean Character generators, world maps, city generators and the like are all geared towards D20 based systems rather then World of darkness, but there are a few things out there, just nothing &quot;Free&quot; persay on-line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9075-mortis","name":"Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}